---
// Literal recreation of the Claude Design canvas's Inventory Staff Support
// Ticket screen (project/StaffTickets.dc.html -> NavSidebar role="staff" +
// NavTop + PageTickets.dc.html) — the same shared --sd-* token shell
// (NavSidebar.astro role="inventory" / NavTop.astro) already established by
// Receiving/Stock Adjustments/Product Lookup, not the old AppShell/
// DESIGN.md Card-based layout this route used to serve (which is why it
// visually read as "the Customer Support Ticket page" — both were built
// from the same generic AppShell/Card components with no role-specific
// design applied).
//
// IMPORTANT — this is the *staff* artboard, not the admin one:
// PageTickets.dc.html (imported by StaffTickets.dc.html, role="staff") is
// a single split-view screen — a real ticket list on the left, the
// selected ticket's detail + an update composer on the right — genuinely
// different from PageAdminTicket.dc.html (imported only by
// AdminTicketDetail.dc.html, a separate admin-only board with a richer
// "Reply to customer" composer, category/assignee-reassignment dropdowns,
// a related-order link and a "Customer's other tickets" panel — none of
// which appear in the staff artboard and none of which are reproduced
// here). Customer's own /account/support/[id] page is a third, separate
// design entirely and was not touched or referenced.
//
// ROUTE: unchanged — this is still the existing /inventory/tickets/[id]
// detail route (same one already linked from Warehouse Tasks' ticket
// rows/topbar action and from NavSidebar/staffSidebarNav's "Support
// tickets" nav item). /inventory/tickets (index) now redirects here for
// the first ticket in whichever tab is active, rather than rendering a
// second, separate list-only page — see that file's own header comment
// for why. No new route, no second support system.
//
// STRUCTURE MATCH: the design's split view (380px ticket list + flexible
// detail/composer) is reproduced on both /inventory/tickets and
// /inventory/tickets/[id] (this file) — the list panel's markup/CSS is
// intentionally duplicated between the two files rather than factored into
// a new shared component, matching this project's existing convention of
// each page owning its own full markup/CSS (see every other .sd-shell
// page). Real tickets, real "Assigned to me"/"Resolved" tabs with real
// counts, real client-side subject search over the real fetched list, real
// status pills (5 real ticket_status values).
//
// NO-FABRICATION DECISIONS (per your explicit instructions — nothing below
// touches support_tickets_messages/attachments/category/order_id, none of
// which exist):
//  - No "TK-1191"-style ticket-number badge: no such id/sequence column
//    exists anywhere in this schema (same reasoning already applied to
//    Stock Adjustments' own Reference column — never invent a "TK-"/"RS-"/
//    "ADJ-" scheme). Each list row leads with its real status pill instead.
//  - "Who reported this" (design shows a customer company/contact name):
//    profiles_select_customers_for_staff/profiles_select_all_for_admin
//    explicitly do NOT grant inventory_staff visibility into another
//    user's profile (confirmed against 0002_profiles_customers.sql) — the
//    reporter's identity is only ever shown when the ticket is
//    self-reported ("Reported by you"); otherwise honestly omitted, never
//    a raw user id.
//  - Category, related order, assignee reassignment, "Customer's other
//    tickets": all admin-only design elements (PageAdminTicket.dc.html),
//    not part of the staff artboard at all — not reproduced, not omitted-
//    as-deferred, simply not applicable here.
//  - "Assigned to you by {name}" banner: no assigner/assigned-by tracking
//    exists on support_tickets — omitted entirely.
//  - Conversation thread: no support_ticket_messages table exists — this
//    is not a real back-and-forth conversation. The design's thread-panel
//    *structure* (bordered scroll area, avatar + name/role/time header,
//    message bubble) is reproduced for exactly the two pieces of real text
//    this ticket actually has: the original report (ticket.description,
//    always present) and, once set, the resolution notes
//    (ticket.resolution) — never a fabricated multi-message exchange,
//    never a fabricated reply, never a fabricated attachment. The design's
//    "Reply to customer"/multi-turn composer is replaced by the one real
//    update path that exists: status + resolution via the unmodified
//    updateSupportTicket action (same as this page always used) — the
//    banner beneath it honestly discloses that direct messaging to the
//    reporter isn't a real capability in this system, rather than
//    reproducing the design's literal (and, for a self-reported ticket,
//    inapplicable) "Admin replies to the customer" copy verbatim.
//  - Status options: kept at all 5 real ticket_status values (open through
//    closed) exactly as the existing updateSupportTicket action/RLS
//    already allow inventory_staff to set on their own assigned tickets —
//    the design's helper text mentions only 3 of the 5 as illustrative
//    example copy for that one example ticket, not a documented business
//    rule anywhere in CLAUDE.md/the action layer, so no new restriction
//    was invented.
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NavSidebar from "../../../components/staff/NavSidebar.astro";
import NavTop from "../../../components/staff/NavTop.astro";

const { id } = Astro.params;
const userId = Astro.locals.user!.id;
const url = Astro.url;
const tab = url.searchParams.get("tab") === "resolved" ? "resolved" : "mine";
const reported = url.searchParams.get("reported");
const updated = url.searchParams.get("updated");

// Real tickets assigned to me — RLS (support_tickets_select_assigned_staff)
// already scopes this to my own assigned rows; filtering explicitly too
// keeps the query's intent readable (same convention used everywhere else
// in this project).
const { data: allTickets } = await Astro.locals.supabase
  .from("support_tickets")
  .select("id, subject, status, created_by, created_at, updated_at")
  .eq("assigned_to", userId)
  .order("updated_at", { ascending: false });

const RESOLVED_STATUSES = new Set(["resolved", "closed"]);
const mineTickets = (allTickets ?? []).filter((t) => !RESOLVED_STATUSES.has(t.status as string));
const resolvedTickets = (allTickets ?? []).filter((t) => RESOLVED_STATUSES.has(t.status as string));
const activeList = tab === "resolved" ? resolvedTickets : mineTickets;
const openTicketCount = mineTickets.length;

// The selected ticket — RLS already scopes this to a ticket assigned to
// me; a ticket assigned to someone else (or a bad id) simply isn't
// returned, same honest 404 treatment this page always used.
const { data: ticket } = await Astro.locals.supabase
  .from("support_tickets")
  .select("id, subject, description, status, resolution, created_by, created_at, updated_at")
  .eq("id", id)
  .maybeSingle();

if (!ticket) {
  Astro.response.status = 404;
}

const isSelfReported = ticket?.created_by === userId;

const STATUS_LABEL: Record<string, string> = {
  open: "Open",
  in_progress: "In Progress",
  waiting: "Waiting",
  resolved: "Resolved",
  closed: "Closed",
};
const STATUS_TONE: Record<string, string> = {
  open: "open",
  in_progress: "progress",
  waiting: "waiting",
  resolved: "resolved",
  closed: "closed",
};
const STATUS_OPTIONS = ["open", "in_progress", "waiting", "resolved", "closed"];

function relativeTime(iso: string): string {
  const diffMs = Date.now() - new Date(iso).getTime();
  const mins = Math.floor(diffMs / 60000);
  if (mins < 1) return "just now";
  if (mins < 60) return `${mins}m ago`;
  const hours = Math.floor(mins / 60);
  if (hours < 24) return `${hours}h ago`;
  const days = Math.floor(hours / 24);
  if (days < 7) return `${days}d ago`;
  return new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString("en-IN", { day: "numeric", month: "short" });
}
function fullTime(iso: string): string {
  return new Date(iso).toLocaleString("en-IN", { day: "numeric", month: "short", hour: "numeric", minute: "2-digit" });
}

function buildUrl(overrides: Record<string, string | undefined>) {
  const next = new URLSearchParams();
  const nextTab = "tab" in overrides ? overrides.tab : tab;
  if (nextTab === "resolved") next.set("tab", "resolved");
  const qs = next.toString();
  return qs ? `?${qs}` : "";
}

const listRows = activeList.map((t) => ({
  id: t.id as string,
  subject: t.subject as string,
  status: t.status as string,
  isSelf: t.created_by === userId,
  updatedAgo: relativeTime(t.updated_at as string),
  href: `/inventory/tickets/${t.id}${buildUrl({})}`,
  isCurrent: t.id === id,
}));
---

<BaseLayout title={ticket ? `${ticket.subject} — Support` : "Ticket not found — Support"}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="sd" id="sd-root">
    <div id="sd-sidebar-backdrop" class="sd__backdrop"></div>

    <div id="sd-sidebar" class="sd__sidebar">
      <NavSidebar active="Support tickets" role="inventory" ticketBadgeCount={openTicketCount} />
    </div>

    <div class="sd__panel">
      <NavTop section="Help" page="Support tickets" />

      <main id="main-content" class="tk__main">
        <div class="tk__header">
          <div class="tk__heading-col">
            <h1>Support tickets</h1>
            <span class="tk__subtitle">Tickets assigned to you</span>
          </div>
          <button type="button" id="tk-report-toggle" class="tk__btn">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" /></svg>
            Report an issue
          </button>
        </div>

        {
          reported && (
            <p class="tk__banner" role="status">
              Issue reported.
            </p>
          )
        }
        {
          updated && (
            <p class="tk__banner" role="status">
              Ticket updated.
            </p>
          )
        }

        <section id="tk-report-panel" class="tk__report-panel" hidden aria-label="Report an issue">
          <h2>Report an issue</h2>
          <p class="tk__report-sub">Reports an operational problem — a note goes to admin for triage.</p>
          <form id="tk-report-form" class="tk__report-form">
            <div class="tk__field-col">
              <label for="tk-report-subject">Subject</label>
              <input type="text" id="tk-report-subject" name="subject" required />
            </div>
            <div class="tk__field-col">
              <label for="tk-report-description">Description</label>
              <textarea id="tk-report-description" name="description" required></textarea>
            </div>
            <p id="tk-report-message" class="tk__status-message" role="status"></p>
            <div class="tk__report-actions">
              <button type="button" id="tk-report-cancel" class="tk__btn">Cancel</button>
              <button type="submit" class="tk__btn tk__btn--primary">Report issue</button>
            </div>
          </form>
        </section>

        <div class="tk__body">
          <section aria-label="Tickets" class="tk__list-panel">
            <div class="tk__list-head">
              <label class="tk__search">
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 11a7 7 0 1 0 14 0a7 7 0 1 0-14 0M20 20l-4-4" /></svg>
                <input type="search" id="tk-search" aria-label="Search tickets" placeholder="Search tickets…" />
              </label>
              <div role="tablist" aria-label="Ticket filter" class="tk__tabs">
                <a href="/inventory/tickets" role="tab" aria-selected={tab === "mine"} class={`tk__tab ${tab === "mine" ? "is-active" : ""}`}>
                  Assigned to me <span class="tk__tab-count">{mineTickets.length}</span>
                </a>
                <a href="/inventory/tickets?tab=resolved" role="tab" aria-selected={tab === "resolved"} class={`tk__tab ${tab === "resolved" ? "is-active" : ""}`}>
                  Resolved <span class="tk__tab-count">{resolvedTickets.length}</span>
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div id="tk-list-scroll" class="tk__list-scroll">
              {
                listRows.length > 0 ? (
                  listRows.map((r) => (
                    <a href={r.href} data-subject={r.subject.toLowerCase()} class={`tk__list-row ${r.isCurrent ? "is-current" : ""}`}>
                      <span class="tk__list-row-top">
                        <span class={`tk__pill tk__pill--${STATUS_TONE[r.status]}`}>{STATUS_LABEL[r.status] ?? r.status}</span>
                        <span class="tk__list-row-time">{r.updatedAgo}</span>
                      </span>
                      <span class="tk__list-row-subject">{r.subject}</span>
                      <span class="tk__list-row-who">{r.isSelf ? "Reported by you" : "—"}</span>
                    </a>
                  ))
                ) : (
                  <p class="tk__list-empty">
                    {tab === "resolved" ? "No resolved tickets." : "No tickets assigned to you."}
                  </p>
                )
              }
            </div>
          </section>

          <section aria-label={ticket ? `Ticket ${ticket.subject}` : "Ticket"} class="tk__detail-panel">
            {
              ticket ? (
                <Fragment>
                  <div class="tk__detail-head">
                    <div class="tk__detail-head-top">
                      <span class={`tk__pill tk__pill--${STATUS_TONE[ticket.status]}`}>{STATUS_LABEL[ticket.status] ?? ticket.status}</span>
                    </div>
                    <h2 class="tk__detail-title">{ticket.subject}</h2>
                    <span class="tk__detail-meta">
                      {isSelfReported ? "Reported by you" : "Reported"} · opened {fullTime(ticket.created_at as string)}
                    </span>
                  </div>

                  <div class="tk__thread">
                    {!isSelfReported && (
                      <div class="tk__thread-banner">
                        You can add operational notes and update status below. Direct messaging to the reporter isn't available in this system yet.
                      </div>
                    )}
                    <article class="tk__msg">
                      <span class="tk__msg-avatar">{isSelfReported ? "You" : "—"}</span>
                      <div class="tk__msg-body">
                        <div class="tk__msg-head">
                          <span class="tk__msg-name">{isSelfReported ? "You" : "Reporter"}</span>
                          <span class="tk__msg-role">Original report</span>
                          <span class="tk__msg-time">{fullTime(ticket.created_at as string)}</span>
                        </div>
                        <p class="tk__msg-text">{ticket.description}</p>
                      </div>
                    </article>
                    {ticket.resolution && (
                      <article class="tk__msg tk__msg--note">
                        <span class="tk__msg-avatar tk__msg-avatar--note">
                          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 11h12v10H6zM8 11V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v4" /></svg>
                        </span>
                        <div class="tk__msg-body">
                          <div class="tk__msg-head">
                            <span class="tk__msg-name">Resolution notes</span>
                            <span class="tk__msg-time">{fullTime(ticket.updated_at as string)}</span>
                          </div>
                          <p class="tk__msg-text">{ticket.resolution}</p>
                        </div>
                      </article>
                    )}
                  </div>

                  <form id="tk-update-form" class="tk__composer">
                    <input type="hidden" name="ticketId" value={ticket.id} />
                    <div class="tk__composer-row">
                      <div class="tk__field-col tk__field-col--status">
                        <label for="tk-status">Status</label>
                        <select id="tk-status" name="status">
                          {STATUS_OPTIONS.map((s) => (
                            <option value={s} selected={ticket.status === s}>{STATUS_LABEL[s]}</option>
                          ))}
                        </select>
                      </div>
                      <span class="tk__composer-hint">Visible to admin — there's no direct messaging to the reporter yet.</span>
                    </div>
                    <textarea id="tk-resolution" name="resolution" class="tk__textarea" placeholder="What did you check or do?">{ticket.resolution ?? ""}</textarea>
                    <p id="tk-form-message" class="tk__status-message" role="status" />
                    <div class="tk__composer-actions">
                      <div class="tk__spacer" />
                      <button type="submit" class="tk__btn tk__btn--primary">
                        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" /></svg>
                        Save update
                      </button>
                    </div>
                  </form>
                </Fragment>
              ) : (
                <div class="tk__empty">
                  <p class="tk__empty-title">Ticket not found</p>
                  <p class="tk__empty-body">It may not be assigned to you.</p>
                </div>
              )
            }
          </section>
        </div>
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sd {
    --sd-shell: #fafafa;
    --sd-panel: #ffffff;
    --sd-card: #ffffff;
    --sd-fg: #0a0a0a;
    --sd-fg2: #404040;
    --sd-muted: #f5f5f5;
    --sd-muted-fg: #737373;
    --sd-border: #e5e5e5;
    --sd-input: #e5e5e5;
    --sd-primary: #171717;
    --sd-primary-fg: #fafafa;
    --sd-success-bg: #ecfdf3;
    --sd-success-fg: #15803d;
    --sd-warn-bg: #fef3e2;
    --sd-warn-fg: #9a3412;
    --sd-danger-bg: #feecec;
    --sd-danger-fg: #b91c1c;
    --sd-info-bg: #eef2ff;
    --sd-info-fg: #3538cd;
    --sd-accent: #2b50e0;
    --sd-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    color-scheme: light;

    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    background: var(--sd-shell);
    color: var(--sd-fg);
    font-family: "Geist", system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .sd[data-theme="dark"] {
    --sd-shell: #0a0a0a;
    --sd-panel: #0f0f0f;
    --sd-card: #171717;
    --sd-fg: #fafafa;
    --sd-fg2: #d4d4d4;
    --sd-muted: #262626;
    --sd-muted-fg: #a3a3a3;
    --sd-border: #262626;
    --sd-input: #363636;
    --sd-primary: #fafafa;
    --sd-primary-fg: #171717;
    --sd-success-bg: #0f2a1c;
    --sd-success-fg: #4ade80;
    --sd-warn-bg: #2e1f0e;
    --sd-warn-fg: #fdba74;
    --sd-danger-bg: #2d1414;
    --sd-danger-fg: #f87171;
    --sd-info-bg: #1e2240;
    --sd-info-fg: #a5b4fc;
    --sd-accent: #6b8afb;
    --sd-shadow: none;
    color-scheme: dark;
  }
  .sd__backdrop {
    display: none;
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
    z-index: 20;
  }
  .sd__sidebar {
    height: 100vh;
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .sd__sidebar {
      position: fixed;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      bottom: 0;
      z-index: 30;
      transform: translateX(-100%);
      transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    }
    .sd__sidebar.is-open {
      transform: translateX(0);
    }
    .sd__backdrop.is-open {
      display: block;
    }
  }
  .sd__panel {
    flex-grow: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    margin: 8px 8px 8px 0;
    background: var(--sd-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--sd-shadow);
  }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .sd__panel {
      margin: 8px;
    }
  }

  .tk__main {
    flex-grow: 1;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 24px 32px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .tk__main {
      padding: 16px;
    }
  }

  .tk__header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .tk__heading-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .tk__heading-col h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }
  .tk__subtitle {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
  }
  .tk__banner {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--sd-success-fg);
  }

  .tk__btn {
    height: 36px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 0 14px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-input);
    background: var(--sd-card);
    color: var(--sd-fg);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .tk__btn--primary {
    border: 0;
    background: var(--sd-primary);
    color: var(--sd-primary-fg);
  }

  .tk__report-panel {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--sd-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sd-shadow);
  }
  .tk__report-panel h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .tk__report-sub {
    margin: 2px 0 12px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
  }
  .tk__report-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    max-width: 460px;
  }
  .tk__field-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .tk__field-col label {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .tk__field-col input[type="text"],
  .tk__report-form textarea {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 8px 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-input);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--sd-card);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--sd-fg);
  }
  .tk__report-form textarea {
    height: 72px;
    resize: vertical;
  }
  .tk__report-actions {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .tk__status-message {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--sd-danger-fg);
    min-height: 0;
  }

  .tk__body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    flex-grow: 1;
    min-height: 0;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1050px) {
    .tk__body {
      flex-direction: row;
    }
  }

  .tk__list-panel {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--sd-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sd-shadow);
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1050px) {
    .tk__list-panel {
      width: 380px;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }
  }
  .tk__list-head {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 12px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sd-border);
  }
  .tk__search {
    height: 36px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 0 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-input);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--sd-card);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
  }
  .tk__search input {
    border: 0;
    outline: 0;
    background: transparent;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 14px;
    flex-grow: 1;
    color: var(--sd-fg);
